    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "Hey, i'm working on a 2022 F-150 that's having some transmission slipping issues. when i hook up the scan tool, i'm seeing a lot of irregular pressure spikes in the hydraulic circuit during the shifts. what are the most likely causes for these kinds of pressure fluctuations?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Those irregular pressure spikes in the hydraulic circuit of your 2022 F-150 transmission are a classic sign of a few things going wrong. It's often related to internal valve body issues, like a sticking or worn solenoid, which is trying to regulate pressure but failing. Another possibility is contamination in the transmission fluid, which can clog passages or cause erratic operation, making the pressure behave unpredictably. You should also check the line pressure and pump output to ensure the system is delivering consistent force.",
